# Data and licence rules

## Sources, licences and etiquette

| Source | Licence | How we use it |
|---|---|---|
| SEC EDGAR XBRL APIs (`frames`, `companyconcept`, `submissions` on data.sec.gov) | US Government work, public domain; SEC fair-access policy | Queried live through Zetaris, never redistributed: no extracted fact values in the repository. Every request carries the declared `User-Agent` from `WON_USER_AGENT`; at most 10 requests per second. Attribution: "Data from SEC EDGAR (sec.gov)". |
| NOAA GHCN-Daily parquet (Registry of Open Data on AWS, `s3://noaa-ghcn-pds`) | CC0 / public domain (US Government work); NOAA asks for attribution | Read anonymously from the public bucket as filestore tables. Attribution: "NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information, Global Historical Climatology Network daily (GHCN-Daily)". |
| company_dns V4 (SIC reference, company-dns.mediumroast.io) | Apache-2.0 | One registration of the SIC code list, called with an identifying `User-Agent`. Attribution to the company_dns project. |

Evidence records carry the endpoint, the licence string, the retrieval time and the Zetaris object.

## What may be committed

- `seeds/utilities.json` and `seeds/stations.json`: CIKs, names, tickers, SIC codes, states served (curated from public service-territory descriptions and labelled curated) and GHCN station ids with state and name. Nothing else from the sources.
- Counts, schemas, object names and timings in `zetaris/README.md` and the docs. Never SEC fact values, filing text or raw API responses; never a GHCN extract (the parquet is public, but `data/` is runtime state and stays gitignored).
- Public numbers (growth, degree days, attribution) come from the agent's own run through Zetaris and appear only in `docs/demo-case.md` and `docs/eval-report.md`, with ranges and labels.
- No personal data: SEC submissions are read for `cik`, `name`, `sic`, `sicDescription` and the business state only, never street fields.

## Code and model licences

- The project is Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE`, `NOTICE`).
- Meterless engines are Apache-2.0 and vendored unchanged; keep their `LICENSE` files and the entry in `NOTICE`.
- `gateway/jdbc.py` is adapted from the Zetaris getting-started repository (Apache-2.0): keep the attribution header and the `NOTICE` entry.
- Scaffolding adapted from the sister project ClearShelf (same author, Apache-2.0) keeps its header note and is listed in `metadata.json` under pre-existing code.
- NVIDIA Nemotron is used under the NVIDIA Open Model License. Model weights are never added to the repository.
